=== attack audit — v4 vs heuristic on W0Base
  100 episodes, win_rate 0.940, 31.1 turns/ep

  attack rate                 1362/4485   0.304 [0.290,0.317]   creatures sent / could have attacked
    reference would send      1145/4485   0.255 [0.243,0.268]   same denominator: the size of any over/under shoot
    reference (CA) would send   944/4485   0.210 [0.199,0.223]
  attack-optimality            786/1264   0.622 [0.595,0.648]   UPPER BOUND: includes no-choice combats
    ...where a choice existed   786/1264   0.622 [0.595,0.648]   the honest one
  attack-optimality (CA)       799/1264   0.632 [0.605,0.658]   reference charges for the crack-back

  score gap (myopic)         3790 over 1264 combats
  score gap (CA)             4167
  missed lethal              1   (own category, never a gap)
  errors UNDER / OVER        277 / 197   (sent fewer / more than ref)
  truncated subsets/replies  1 / 0
  combats with no choice     0   (MATCH there is the position's)

  cost: policy search 0 ms total, 0.00 ms/combat; audit 500201 ms (instrument, not play)
  nodes: 0k resolve() calls, 0 per combat

  READ WITH: the reference is one combat deep and prices at zero
  the fact that an attacker cannot block next turn, so it
  over-credits attacking. A rise in attack-optimality alongside
  a rise in attack rate is partly tautological; the CA row and
  the UNDER/OVER split are what separate them.
